// Types are `behavior`, `script`, `application`, `library`, `testcase`, `component`, `trait`
// See the documentation for more information.
behavior ${name}
    "Describe this behavior"
    // version number is mandatory. Do not forget to change it when the actor changes API.
    version 1.0
    // declare all imported agents here
    using core.console as console

// the init action is optional and can be seen as the constructor of the agent. If it has
// parameters, an agent will need to pass them to the `new` verb when creating an agent.
// Scripts, applications and test cases parameters do not normally have parameters, but
// they can be used to pass parameters through the command line if executed from a shell.
action init:
    // here you define the global agent's state, if any is needed. You can only use
    // the `def` verb in the `init` action. The global state is visible to other agents.
    def name "${name}"

// the main action is optional: it will execute automatically (after 'init') if present
action main:
    // Add behavior statements here. At least one statement is mandatory
    console.format("Hello from %s\n", name)

// the @stdin annotation binds the following action to the console input stream
@stdin
action input(message, sender):
    // Add input handling here.
    console.format("Received message: %s\n", message)

// the @handle annotation binds the following action to a specific message class. Other
// agents (or the agent debugger) can send messages of this class to the agent. The
// parameters are bound to the payload; the `sender` parameter is reserved for the
// agent sending the message.
@handle(class=SAYHELLO)
action sayhello(message, sender):
    console.format("Agent says hello: %s\n", message)